## Data Model (Postgres, all RLS-enabled)

- **profiles** (1:1 `auth.users`): `name`, `surname`, `avatar_url`, `notification_prior_meeting`, `notification_reminder_interval`. (No `username` — was dropped.)
- **push_tokens**: `user_id` PK, `token`. Separate table so only owner reads it; Edge Functions read all via `service_role`.
- **push_token_events**: diagnostic log written via `log_push_token_event` RPC.
- **board_games**: `name`, `description`, `genre`, `min_players`, `max_players`, `tutorial_url`, `spotify_playlist_url`, `image_url`, `owners` (text[]).
- **meetings**: `number`, `status`, `chosen_date`, `chosen_game_id`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `voting_start_date`.
- **date_options**: `meeting_id`, `date`, `is_custom`, `added_by`.
- **votes** (one per user per meeting) → **vote_dates** (`date_option_id`) + **vote_games** (`game_id`).
- **survey_reminder_log**: per-user `sent_at` for reminder throttling.

Canonical TS types live in `lib/types.ts`. Key SQL functions: `create_next_survey()`, `get_consecutive_game_count()`, Polish-holidays computation (mirrored in `lib/holidays.ts`).

## Edge Functions (`supabase/functions/`)

Cron (daily): `create-survey`, `survey-reminder`, `meeting-reminder`, `complete-meeting`.
Trigger-based push: `notify-survey-created`, `notify-meeting-approved`, `notify-meeting-unapproved`.
User-invoked: `delete-account` (GDPR self-service: verifies caller JWT, removes their avatar + deletes the auth user, cascading profile/memberships/votes). `verify_jwt` on (not in `config.toml`).
Shared push sender: `_shared/push.ts` (Expo Push API, batches of 100). Excluded from app tsconfig (Deno runtime).

## Conventions & Gotchas

- **Realtime**: `meetings` + `votes` tables published; subscribe for live voter counts / approval changes. Use `useFocusEffect` to refetch on screen focus.
- **Storage**: private buckets `avatars`, `game-images`. Never store raw paths in UI — use `useSignedUrl` / `useSignedUrls` (`lib/storage.ts`, auto-refresh before 1h expiry). Delete old image on replace/delete to avoid orphans.
- **Alerts**: use `showAlert` from `lib/alert.ts` (cross-platform; web falls back to `window.alert/confirm`), not `Alert.alert` directly.
- **Strings**: all user-facing text via `t("…")`; add keys to BOTH `lib/i18n/en.ts` and `pl.ts`.
- **Web**: guard native-only features (`expo-calendar`, push) with `Platform.OS === "web"`. Web is centered max-width 700px.
- **Theme**: warm wood palette — bg `#fdf8f0`, headers `#4a3228`, tabs `#3d2818`, accent amber `#f59e0b`, light text `#fef3c7`.
- **Security**: anon key + RLS is the boundary (repo is public-safe). `service_role` only in Edge Functions. `.env` and `supabase/config.toml` gitignored.
- **Migrations**: never edit historical ones — add a new file. See `supabase-migrations.mdc` for required grants/RLS pattern.
- **Minimum supported version (force-update gate)**: implemented — remote `min_version` in the `app_config` table (Supabase, public read), checked on startup by `lib/version.ts`; outdated native builds are hard-blocked with an "Update required" screen (`components/UpdateRequiredScreen.tsx`, wired in `app/_layout.tsx`). Web is exempt; fails open on error. **Breaking-change rule**: for every change, check whether it breaks backward compatibility between backend and app (DB/RLS/schema/edge-function change, or removed client behavior). If it does: bump the app `version` in `app.config.ts` on the release that fixes it, and once that build is live raise `app_config.min_version` (via dashboard or a new migration) to lock out older clients. The two versions must move together (a shipped build's `version` must be ≥ the `min_version` you set). See `docs/version-gate.md`.
- **Git**: never commit/push without explicit user instruction; never to main/master.

> Note: `README.md` and `.cursor/plans/boardgames_meeting_planner_a7addda3.plan.md` give origin design intent but predate some changes (e.g. `username` removal, the trigger-based `notify-*` functions). Trust the code/`lib/types.ts` when they disagree.

## Keeping This File Up To Date

When a change materially alters anything described above, update this rule in the same change. Triggers include: new/removed/renamed screen or route; new/changed DB table, column, or key SQL function; added/removed Edge Function or its trigger/schedule; new shared `lib/` utility or convention; stack/dependency or tooling shift; theme/palette change. Skip purely internal refactors that don't change the domain, data model, screens, or conventions.

